{"task_id": "Mbpp/4", "solution": "import heapq\n\ndef heap_queue_largest(numbers: list[int], n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the n largest integers from a list, returned in descending order.\n    Handles edge cases like n <= 0, empty list, and n > list size.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0 or not numbers:\n        return []\n\n    # Use heapq.nlargest for efficiency. It handles the min-heap logic internally.\n    # It returns items in order from largest to smallest.\n    largest_elements = heapq.nlargest(n, numbers)\n\n    return largest_elements"}
