{"task_id": "Mbpp/20", "solution": "def is_woodall(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is a Woodall number.\n    A Woodall number is of the form n * 2^n - 1 for some integer n >= 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 0:\n        return False\n\n    n = 1\n    while True:\n        woodall_candidate = n * (2**n) - 1\n        if woodall_candidate == number:\n            return True\n        elif woodall_candidate > number:\n            return False\n        n += 1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "class Number:\n    def __init__(self, value: int):\n        self.value = value\n\n    def reverse_value(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Returns the decimal reverse of the number.\"\"\"\n        sign = -1 if self.value < 0 else 1\n        rev = int(str(abs(self.value))[::-1])\n        return sign * rev\n\n\ndef check(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is one less than twice its reverse.\"\"\"\n    num = Number(number)\n    rev = num.reverse_value()\n    return number == 2 * rev - 1"}
