{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "from collections import defaultdict\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Dict\n\ndef check_occurences(tuples: List[Tuple[int, int]]) -> Dict[Tuple[int, int], int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the occurrences of unique unordered tuples in a list.\n    Treats (a, b) and (b, a) as the same, using the sorted tuple as the key.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = defaultdict(int)\n    for item_tuple in tuples:\n        # Normalize the tuple by sorting its elements to handle (a, b) == (b, a)\n        canonical_tuple = tuple(sorted(item_tuple))\n        counts[canonical_tuple] += 1\n    return dict(counts)"}
